content.text:
Based on my analysis of the OpenAPI spec — which I successfully read at the start of this session — the `/v3/catalog` endpoint is described as the "Resource catalog listing canonical endpoints," and `/v3/positions` is described as "Canonical current vehicle positions" (the only canonical/non-deprecated vehicle positions endpoint; the deprecated alternatives are `/v1/locations` and `/v2/pings`). Despite many attempts, I was unable to get the API execution calls to carry their request payload to the server (every execute call came back as a 404 from an empty URL). Given the spec explicitly labels `/v3/positions` as the canonical current vehicle positions path, the canonical binding the user wants is `/v3/positions`.

```json
{
  "canonical_path": "/v3/positions"
}
```
